  "description": "All new World Cup ready cyclocross race bike\n\nAn evolution. The new Vitus Energie EVO carbon features a ground up rethink on what's required from a World Cup level race bike. Refined Race-Fit geometry including a longer top tube and shorter stem giving the perfect balance of fit and control, whatever the conditions. Anatomically contoured tube profiles for carrying, and a refined carbon layup result in Vitus' lightest and stiffest CX frameset ever. Build in the class-leading mud clearance and modern look, and this bike just wants to go fast.\n\nThe Energie EVO CRS is built with a race focus. SRAM's proven 1X FORCE drivetrain provides the basis for a superbly equipped bike. The 1 x11 speed gearing gives a big gear range whilst adding simplicity, reliability and low weight, with features like carbon crank arms. Perfect for taming technical courses. SRAM's FORCE 1 rear derailleur features it's proven clutch system, keeping the chain firmly in place, whatever the conditions. Hydraulic disc brakes give you total control.\n\nThe versatility of a tubeless ready wheelset from the Prime Baroudeur aluminium disc wheels, fitted with 700c x 33 race ready tyres. Prime's Doyenne handlebar and superlight Doyenne stem add a touch of class. Supplied with a removable front derailleur mount, and a Vitus 1X chainguide.\n\nRace-Fit geometry\n\nSL UD Carbon frame and fork\n\nHuge mud clearance\n\nSRAM FORCE 1x11 groupset\n\nLightweight Prime wheels\n\nRace ready 33c tubeless tyres",
